  "description": "PESTOZ crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n m c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H100 Cr2 O28 Y3 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 9 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 9 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.439-3.944 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.55-110.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H116Cr2NY3O28.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
